      "notes_html": "<p>Between Chastelen and Tomlishorn there are faint paths in the scree, followed by an exposed traverse on a one meter wide ledge and at the end some scrambling passages (fixed ropes). As the route lies mainly in the shadow, it is often wet (thus precarious), and in the spring you encounter treacherous fields of old snow.</p>"
